  "decision_agency": null,
  "subdivision_of_building": "Part of first and second floor",
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "cil_liability": true,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed flats, by reason of indequate daylight and sunlight provision, inadequate outlook from the first floor creating an undue sense of enclosure, poor quality natural ventilation and the inherent risk of overheating and poor internal air quality, would consitute a substandard form of residential accommodation, to the detriment of the living conditions of future residents. The proposal would accordingly fail to comply with Policy D6 of the London Plan, Kingston's Residential Design SPD and Chapter 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "The proposal would result in the loss of Class E floorspace within the New Malden District Centre, failing to protect existing employment land and premises and the applicant has failed to produce sound evidence and rigorous marketing to demonstrate that a reasonable effort to make the space suitable for commercial occupants or demonstrated a genuine intent to use the space for commercial uses. The proposal would accordingly fail to comply with Policies DM17, CS11 and CS12 of the Kingston Core Strategy and Chapter 7 of the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
